1
00:00:07,560 --> 00:00:08,920
SAY NO TO PIRACY, SUPPORT ORIGINALS

2
00:01:36,680 --> 00:01:38,800
ADAPTED FROM <i>THE EARLY SPRING</i> ON JJWXC.NET
AUTHOR: GU NIANG BIE KU

3
00:01:52,960 --> 00:01:54,000
Lumi.

4
00:01:54,880 --> 00:01:55,840
I want to work in this place.

5
00:01:59,400 --> 00:02:01,080
NORTHWESTERN CULTURAL TOURISM
DEVELOPMENT PROJECT, BUSINESS DIVISION ONE

6
00:02:03,000 --> 00:02:04,360
Northwestern China?

7
00:02:04,440 --> 00:02:06,040
That's so far away from here.

8
00:02:06,120 --> 00:02:09,440
And the project will run
for 14 months, not 14 days.

9
00:02:11,280 --> 00:02:13,520
I know. But I have made up my mind.

10
00:02:14,200 --> 00:02:15,400
Tracy told me that

11
00:02:15,480 --> 00:02:18,000
while I passed all the requirements,
I still needed a bit more.

12
00:02:18,520 --> 00:02:20,200
I have never managed
any S+ projects of highly importance.

13
00:02:20,280 --> 00:02:22,240
This is a great opportunity.

14
00:02:22,320 --> 00:02:23,400
It's all I need now.

15
00:02:30,440 --> 00:02:31,920
Same here.

16
00:02:39,960 --> 00:02:41,360
You have not given up yet?

17
00:02:42,520 --> 00:02:44,360
The boy is mine.

18
00:02:44,880 --> 00:02:46,200
He saved my life.

19
00:02:46,960 --> 00:02:49,600
It's only right for me to marry him.

20
00:02:50,200 --> 00:02:53,520
What? When did he save your life?

21
00:02:55,240 --> 00:02:57,880
My ex harassed me a while ago.

22
00:02:57,960 --> 00:02:59,280
We almost got physical.

23
00:02:59,360 --> 00:03:02,080
And he suddenly appeared to save me.

24
00:03:02,760 --> 00:03:05,920
He fought two enemies alone,
and he did not lose.

25
00:03:06,000 --> 00:03:10,280
So manly. He looks like a nerd,

26
00:03:10,360 --> 00:03:12,360
but how can he be
so handsome when he fights?

27
00:03:12,440 --> 00:03:15,000
His abs. His posture. I was like…

28
00:03:22,720 --> 00:03:23,800
Did he look at me?

29
00:03:24,920 --> 00:03:25,760
Did he look at me?

30
00:03:28,600 --> 00:03:29,840
He did.

31
00:03:47,000 --> 00:03:50,120
ANOTHER LEAP OF FAITH

32
00:03:59,120 --> 00:04:00,120
Come in.

33
00:04:03,320 --> 00:04:04,440
Luke.

34
00:04:06,080 --> 00:04:06,920
Take a seat.

35
00:04:13,160 --> 00:04:14,000
Luke.

36
00:04:16,600 --> 00:04:18,880
I would like to apply
to join the Northwestern

37
00:04:18,959 --> 00:04:21,040
Cultural Tourism
Development Project team next month.

38
00:04:23,600 --> 00:04:24,800
That is a tough subject.

39
00:04:25,400 --> 00:04:27,160
You only return here
for two days per month.

40
00:04:28,760 --> 00:04:29,840
Still, I want to join.

41
00:04:30,640 --> 00:04:31,520
Why?

42
00:04:33,200 --> 00:04:35,600
Because I believe we all have a value
and a place we need to be.

43
00:04:35,680 --> 00:04:37,760
Where there is a risk,
there is an opportunity too.

44
00:04:38,360 --> 00:04:40,760
I'm still young. I want to take the risk.

45
00:04:40,840 --> 00:04:43,480
I'm also aware
that given my average skills,

46
00:04:43,560 --> 00:04:45,440
I won't be able to pick up an S+ project

47
00:04:45,520 --> 00:04:47,560
unless it is very far away.

48
00:04:50,080 --> 00:04:53,200
Shang Zhitao, you won't admit this,

49
00:04:53,920 --> 00:04:55,160
but you are selling yourself short.

50
00:04:55,240 --> 00:04:57,680
You want to tread off the beaten path

51
00:04:59,080 --> 00:05:01,160
and hope it may lead to success.

52
00:05:03,000 --> 00:05:05,600
But someone has to make
the path first, right?

53
00:05:05,680 --> 00:05:09,280
No one wants to make this path, but I do.

54
00:05:10,040 --> 00:05:12,000
Luke. Can you approve it?

55
00:05:12,680 --> 00:05:14,360
This is also on my wishlist.

56
00:05:17,040 --> 00:05:19,040
I have a wishlist.

57
00:05:22,720 --> 00:05:25,040
I really want the expert title.

58
00:05:32,680 --> 00:05:33,520
Fine.

59
00:05:34,200 --> 00:05:35,040
As you wish.

60
00:05:37,000 --> 00:05:37,920
Okay.

61
00:05:38,000 --> 00:05:38,920
Thanks.

62
00:05:41,480 --> 00:05:42,600
What about Luke then?

63
00:05:49,280 --> 00:05:50,200
I haven't thought about it.

64
00:05:50,280 --> 00:05:51,560
When push comes to shove,
I'll bring him with me.

65
00:05:54,960 --> 00:05:56,160
You can let him live with me.

66
00:05:57,200 --> 00:05:58,720
He knows my place well anyway.

67
00:06:01,400 --> 00:06:02,760
I wouldn't want to trouble you,
But thanks.

68
00:06:26,880 --> 00:06:27,840
So…

69
00:06:29,440 --> 00:06:30,600
You broke up?

70
00:06:32,520 --> 00:06:33,400
I don't know.

71
00:06:36,080 --> 00:06:37,480
I guess so.

72
00:06:38,480 --> 00:06:42,280
He rejected me,
but I wasn't embarrassed or anything.

73
00:06:43,080 --> 00:06:44,280
And I do not resent him either.

74
00:06:45,120 --> 00:06:48,320
Now I've become an emotionless workaholic.

75
00:06:52,360 --> 00:06:54,200
Perhaps you didn't love him that much.

76
00:06:55,600 --> 00:06:56,760
Or perhaps

77
00:06:58,560 --> 00:07:00,680
a true heartbreak is always silent.

78
00:07:03,920 --> 00:07:05,560
Or perhaps…

79
00:07:10,760 --> 00:07:13,680
Or perhaps we have never fallen in love.

80
00:07:20,280 --> 00:07:22,760
Even though we were in a relationship,

81
00:07:24,920 --> 00:07:26,200
it was never real.

82
00:07:33,040 --> 00:07:34,320
I don't think it's gastric.

83
00:07:35,800 --> 00:07:37,600
I just feel a bit bloated.

84
00:07:39,040 --> 00:07:41,920
Wait. Are you still with that girl?

85
00:07:42,520 --> 00:07:44,680
<i>Did you use protection?</i>

86
00:07:45,440 --> 00:07:46,360
What are you saying?

87
00:07:47,040 --> 00:07:47,880
Just be frank.

88
00:07:47,960 --> 00:07:49,280
All right then.

89
00:07:49,360 --> 00:07:51,560
Did you contract any STDs?

90
00:07:53,360 --> 00:07:55,480
I'm about to be as chaste as a monk.

91
00:08:04,200 --> 00:08:06,200
SHANG ZHITAO

92
00:08:10,080 --> 00:08:11,120
Yes?

93
00:08:11,640 --> 00:08:15,960
<i>Is Luke's rabies</i>
<i>vaccine certificate with you?</i>

94
00:08:18,400 --> 00:08:20,520
Yes. I have it.

95
00:08:22,000 --> 00:08:24,200
But I'm sick now. I can't go out.

96
00:08:25,280 --> 00:08:26,240
Why don't you drop by my place?

97
00:08:27,360 --> 00:08:29,440
Get me some medicine.
I'll send the brand to you.

98
00:08:52,680 --> 00:08:53,680
Luke.

99
00:08:59,800 --> 00:09:00,680
Are you okay?

100
00:09:00,760 --> 00:09:02,880
Where does it hurt? You're in pain.

101
00:09:02,960 --> 00:09:04,280
Are you sure the medicine will help?

102
00:09:04,360 --> 00:09:05,400
Let's go to the hospital.

103
00:09:08,080 --> 00:09:09,560
I don't like hospitals.

104
00:09:16,400 --> 00:09:17,640
It hurts so much.

105
00:09:18,320 --> 00:09:19,440
I can't find the vaccine certificate.

106
00:09:23,600 --> 00:09:25,200
It's too late for you to get one anyway.

107
00:09:27,480 --> 00:09:31,000
I don't like to owe anyone a favor.
Given that you brought medicine for me,

108
00:09:32,800 --> 00:09:33,720
fine,

109
00:09:34,240 --> 00:09:35,440
I'll take care of Luke for you.

110
00:09:36,800 --> 00:09:39,360
You… You're sick,

111
00:09:39,440 --> 00:09:41,760
And I've already checked your schedule.

112
00:09:41,840 --> 00:09:43,800
You have a business trip next week.

113
00:09:44,840 --> 00:09:46,680
Your flatmates also have business trips.

114
00:09:47,520 --> 00:09:49,320
Besides, my neighborhood
has a dedicated dog sitter.

115
00:10:02,960 --> 00:10:05,560
NORTHWESTERN CHINA

116
00:10:05,640 --> 00:10:06,680
Sun Yuanzhu.

117
00:10:07,760 --> 00:10:09,760
You have lost a lot of weight.

118
00:10:09,840 --> 00:10:11,800
Is the food here that bad?

119
00:10:13,400 --> 00:10:15,040
No, it's good.

120
00:10:15,120 --> 00:10:16,880
I have been busy, that's all.

121
00:10:18,160 --> 00:10:19,600
Then, I shouldn't have
asked you to pick me up.

122
00:10:19,680 --> 00:10:21,000
No way.

123
00:10:21,800 --> 00:10:24,280
Tao. I'm so happy that you're here.

124
00:10:25,560 --> 00:10:28,920
Following your footsteps,
I have come here to achieve my ambition.

125
00:10:29,000 --> 00:10:33,920
I, Ms. Shang Zhitao,
will be working with the local councils

126
00:10:34,520 --> 00:10:37,280
as the project director of Lime.

127
00:10:37,360 --> 00:10:42,040
I will combine the local culture
and digital technology

128
00:10:42,120 --> 00:10:45,040
to develop a new cultural tourism.
What do you think? Is that impressive?

129
00:10:45,680 --> 00:10:48,520
Ms. Shang Zhitao,
you have become a bigwig.

130
00:10:48,600 --> 00:10:49,520
Yes.

131
00:10:51,520 --> 00:10:54,600
May your project
become a huge success soon.

132
00:10:54,680 --> 00:10:56,880
May your self-driving car

133
00:10:58,200 --> 00:11:00,000
go on the street soon.

134
00:11:01,040 --> 00:11:02,080
Okay.

135
00:11:05,920 --> 00:11:09,400
Sun Yuanzhu. This is such
a special mountain range.

136
00:11:10,680 --> 00:11:12,560
It's the spine of a dragon.

137
00:11:14,240 --> 00:11:15,320
A dragon spine?

138
00:11:35,040 --> 00:11:36,640
<i>When I asked</i>
<i>to take on this distant project,</i>

139
00:11:36,720 --> 00:11:38,160
<i>some said it was beyond my capability.</i>

140
00:11:38,240 --> 00:11:39,520
<i>Some said I was trying</i>
<i>too hard to impress.</i>

141
00:11:40,040 --> 00:11:43,000
<i>But I know very well</i>
<i>that when I look down,</i>

142
00:11:43,720 --> 00:11:45,640
<i>it is to make sure</i>
<i>I am walking the right path.</i>

143
00:11:46,680 --> 00:11:47,600
<i>I'm so glad I'm here.</i>

144
00:11:48,120 --> 00:11:50,640
NORTHWESTERN CHINA LAND LAW DRAFT

145
00:12:15,360 --> 00:12:17,640
SECTION EIGHT
PROPERTY OWNERSHIP RESOLUTION

146
00:12:18,280 --> 00:12:20,080
<i>I used to think working</i>

147
00:12:20,160 --> 00:12:22,320
<i>was drinking with the right person</i>
<i>at a business dinner.</i>

148
00:12:22,840 --> 00:12:24,160
<i>But now I learned</i>

149
00:12:24,680 --> 00:12:27,760
<i>that the real battle</i>
<i>takes place where no one is around.</i>

150
00:12:29,440 --> 00:12:31,800
THREE MONTHS LATER

151
00:12:36,080 --> 00:12:37,760
It represents our ideal.

152
00:12:40,400 --> 00:12:41,440
- Our idea…
- Flora.

153
00:12:41,520 --> 00:12:43,400
Mr. Luan has arrived. Come.

154
00:12:43,480 --> 00:12:44,360
Okay.

155
00:13:00,360 --> 00:13:01,920
- Flora.
- Lumi.

156
00:13:03,320 --> 00:13:04,640
I've missed you.

157
00:13:07,760 --> 00:13:08,760
Allow me to introduce.

158
00:13:10,280 --> 00:13:12,120
This is Flora, our project director
in Northwestern China.

159
00:13:12,840 --> 00:13:14,600
Flora. Our new colleague.

160
00:13:14,680 --> 00:13:15,560
Yilia.

161
00:13:16,160 --> 00:13:18,000
Flora. We finally meet.

162
00:13:18,080 --> 00:13:19,920
People have been
praising you at the office.

163
00:13:20,000 --> 00:13:20,960
I can't wait to learn from you.

164
00:13:21,040 --> 00:13:22,240
Likewise.

165
00:13:23,440 --> 00:13:25,560
It's about time. Come in.

166
00:13:33,080 --> 00:13:34,320
She's an elite who joined our division

167
00:13:34,400 --> 00:13:36,560
all the way
from the headquarters in the US.

168
00:13:37,080 --> 00:13:38,160
She bought her way in.

169
00:13:39,240 --> 00:13:41,440
Is this project that important?

170
00:13:41,520 --> 00:13:43,160
Even a bigwig like her is here.

171
00:13:44,080 --> 00:13:46,320
Of course, you have
an influential figure backing you up.

172
00:13:46,840 --> 00:13:48,760
Luke's presence is the greatest privilege
you can have.

173
00:13:49,600 --> 00:13:50,440
And I'm here too.

174
00:13:51,720 --> 00:13:52,680
Come.

175
00:13:53,400 --> 00:13:55,920
We like dragons. We deify dragons.

176
00:13:56,000 --> 00:13:57,960
Dragons are like our ideals.

177
00:13:58,040 --> 00:14:00,480
Our idea should incorporate
this kind of ideal.

178
00:14:00,560 --> 00:14:03,440
Instead of focusing on the landscape,

179
00:14:03,520 --> 00:14:07,560
we should highlight
the generations that live here.

180
00:14:07,640 --> 00:14:10,440
There are sculptures.
There is cultural heritage.

181
00:14:11,480 --> 00:14:14,720
So what exactly is Northwestern China?

182
00:14:24,000 --> 00:14:26,120
NORTHWESTERN CULTURAL TOURISM

183
00:14:26,200 --> 00:14:27,560
TARGET AUDIENCES
WELLNESS SEEKERS & FAMILY TRAVELERS

184
00:14:27,640 --> 00:14:28,280
TRENDY YOUTH & NICHE EXPLORERS

185
00:14:36,600 --> 00:14:37,800
PRIMARY PALETTE & ITS IMPACT

186
00:14:54,360 --> 00:14:56,280
That's all for my presentation.

187
00:14:56,360 --> 00:14:57,600
Thank you for listening.

188
00:15:10,200 --> 00:15:11,800
Please proceed to the lounge next to us.

189
00:15:11,880 --> 00:15:13,960
We have prepared food and refreshments.

190
00:15:23,640 --> 00:15:25,400
I have taught Flora well.

191
00:15:25,480 --> 00:15:27,040
She made me proud.

192
00:15:28,320 --> 00:15:29,480
She's so good.

193
00:15:29,560 --> 00:15:32,800
She recognizes, values,
and manages talents very well.

194
00:15:32,880 --> 00:15:33,840
She can do everything.

195
00:15:34,640 --> 00:15:37,240
Flora is indeed exceptional in Lime.

196
00:15:38,160 --> 00:15:40,360
She started from a humble background.
She has a clear goal

197
00:15:40,960 --> 00:15:41,880
and works hard.

198
00:15:42,440 --> 00:15:45,160
Her amicability is also
one of a kind in Lime.

199
00:15:45,240 --> 00:15:48,160
Many colleagues remarked
that her passion and honesty

200
00:15:49,080 --> 00:15:50,560
were exemplary attributes.

201
00:15:51,520 --> 00:15:52,560
You're a smooth-talker today.

202
00:15:58,440 --> 00:15:59,760
Go eat first.

203
00:16:00,280 --> 00:16:01,520
I'll talk to Flora for a while.

204
00:16:02,400 --> 00:16:03,680
Come. Let's eat.

205
00:16:09,000 --> 00:16:10,000
NORTHWESTERN CULTURAL TOURISM
CONFERENCE HALL, BREAK ROOM

206
00:16:21,000 --> 00:16:22,280
Are you okay?

207
00:16:25,280 --> 00:16:26,320
It hurts.

208
00:16:36,600 --> 00:16:39,000
Stop moving around. Okay?

209
00:16:39,080 --> 00:16:40,040
Sit properly.

210
00:16:42,320 --> 00:16:43,680
You'll be fine soon.

211
00:16:46,160 --> 00:16:48,200
Am I going to die here?

212
00:16:48,280 --> 00:16:49,480
What are you on about?

213
00:16:50,000 --> 00:16:51,320
This is a good hospital.

214
00:16:51,400 --> 00:16:53,200
Besides, I'm here.

215
00:16:57,120 --> 00:16:58,080
Are you thirsty?

216
00:17:04,079 --> 00:17:07,839
The doctor said
you shouldn't drink soda anymore.

217
00:17:07,920 --> 00:17:10,960
Once we're back, I'll throw away
your cola and soda.

218
00:17:11,480 --> 00:17:12,400
Are you hungry?

219
00:17:16,079 --> 00:17:17,319
It's just a kidney stone.

220
00:17:17,960 --> 00:17:19,200
I'm fine.

221
00:17:21,119 --> 00:17:22,839
Just a kidney stone?

222
00:17:22,920 --> 00:17:24,720
You're the one suffering here.

223
00:17:36,280 --> 00:17:38,160
Does it not hurt anymore?
Why are you smiling?

224
00:17:40,920 --> 00:17:41,920
Lie down.

225
00:18:53,160 --> 00:18:54,440
Don't tell Lumi and the rest.

226
00:18:57,920 --> 00:18:59,000
Just tell them I went back to Beijing.

227
00:18:59,840 --> 00:19:01,120
You won't stay at the hotel?

228
00:19:03,240 --> 00:19:05,560
No. I'm staying with you.

229
00:19:07,560 --> 00:19:09,000
I need a carer.

230
00:19:41,320 --> 00:19:42,240
Yes.

231
00:19:42,320 --> 00:19:43,200
It's not out yet.

232
00:19:44,080 --> 00:19:46,040
I had an X-ray yesterday.
The doctor said it was moving out.

233
00:19:47,440 --> 00:19:49,200
It'll come out if I raise
my calves or climb stairs more often.

234
00:19:51,880 --> 00:19:53,120
Don't worry.

235
00:19:53,200 --> 00:19:54,240
Someone is looking after me.

236
00:19:56,320 --> 00:19:57,320
Who, you asked?

237
00:19:59,000 --> 00:19:59,840
My girlfriend.

238
00:20:01,840 --> 00:20:02,960
<i>Your girlfriend?</i>

239
00:20:03,720 --> 00:20:05,560
Can I speak to her?

240
00:20:06,160 --> 00:20:08,760
I need to talk to her
about your condition.

241
00:20:10,000 --> 00:20:12,640
<i>Or maybe I should fly</i>
<i>to Northwestern China and drag you back?</i>

242
00:20:12,720 --> 00:20:14,720
You want to speak to my girlfriend?

243
00:20:15,320 --> 00:20:16,320
Okay.

244
00:20:17,400 --> 00:20:18,240
It's my mom.

245
00:20:18,960 --> 00:20:20,120
She thinks I have a terminal illness.

246
00:20:24,440 --> 00:20:25,720
Hi, Dr. Liang.

247
00:20:26,320 --> 00:20:27,200
Hi.

248
00:20:27,840 --> 00:20:29,680
Miss, how should I address you?

249
00:20:29,760 --> 00:20:31,200
Just call me Flora.

250
00:20:32,080 --> 00:20:33,120
<i>Flora.</i>

251
00:20:33,200 --> 00:20:34,760
I just want to know
about Luan Nian's condition.

252
00:20:35,360 --> 00:20:37,360
<i>Is it true that he has a kidney stone?</i>

253
00:20:38,400 --> 00:20:40,560
Yes, he has a kidney stone.

254
00:20:40,640 --> 00:20:41,680
Don't worry about him.

255
00:20:41,760 --> 00:20:45,840
<i>Luke has already told you</i>
<i>what he needed to do.</i>

256
00:20:45,920 --> 00:20:48,040
I'll take him
to get his X-ray done in a few days.

257
00:20:48,560 --> 00:20:49,400
So don't worry about it.

258
00:20:50,360 --> 00:20:51,360
Okay.

259
00:20:52,440 --> 00:20:55,480
Flora. I know Luan Nian has a bad temper

260
00:20:55,560 --> 00:20:56,760
<i>and he can be quite weird.</i>

261
00:20:56,840 --> 00:20:58,560
- <i>But don't--</i>
- Anyway,

262
00:20:58,640 --> 00:21:01,200
as you already know, I'm not dead.
I'm hanging up now.

263
00:21:04,400 --> 00:21:06,280
Make sure to take your medicine.
I have to work now.

264
00:21:08,280 --> 00:21:09,800
When are you coming back?

265
00:21:11,400 --> 00:21:12,480
As soon as possible.

266
00:21:51,760 --> 00:21:53,640
Why are you lying on the couch?

267
00:21:54,400 --> 00:21:55,320
You're back.

268
00:22:01,400 --> 00:22:02,360
The mattress is too firm.

269
00:22:03,400 --> 00:22:05,640
The comforter is not soft enough.
And it's too thick.

270
00:22:06,240 --> 00:22:07,520
The pillow is too low.

271
00:22:09,000 --> 00:22:10,160
Are you a princess or what?

272
00:22:12,240 --> 00:22:13,920
You know what?
I'll get you a room in a hotel.

273
00:22:14,000 --> 00:22:15,560
But you won't stay
in the same hotel as Lumi.

274
00:22:15,640 --> 00:22:16,640
Is that okay?

275
00:22:17,760 --> 00:22:19,160
No.

276
00:22:19,240 --> 00:22:21,200
I just feel quite weak.

277
00:22:21,280 --> 00:22:22,280
It hurts everywhere.

278
00:22:23,920 --> 00:22:26,240
I'll just rest in the room. I'll lie down.

279
00:22:36,400 --> 00:22:37,920
Maybe you should return to Beijing.

280
00:22:38,440 --> 00:22:40,080
They have big hospitals there.

281
00:22:40,160 --> 00:22:41,600
You won't have to wait as long.

282
00:22:41,680 --> 00:22:42,880
I can't go back.

283
00:22:42,960 --> 00:22:44,360
Even getting out of bed
takes a lot of effort.

284
00:22:44,440 --> 00:22:45,680
I need time to recover.

285
00:22:47,520 --> 00:22:49,200
I bought a free-range chicken.

286
00:22:49,280 --> 00:22:50,560
Should I cook it for you?

287
00:22:55,280 --> 00:22:56,520
Are you sure I won't be poisoned?

288
00:22:57,920 --> 00:22:59,440
I can assure you
that it will be cooked thoroughly.

289
00:23:00,520 --> 00:23:03,480
You will do it an injustice
if it's not delicious enough.

290
00:23:08,200 --> 00:23:09,240
Let me cook.

291
00:23:11,600 --> 00:23:13,760
You… Aren't you sick?

292
00:23:15,720 --> 00:23:16,600
I can hang in there.

293
00:23:28,880 --> 00:23:29,840
Come. Drink some soup.

294
00:23:33,280 --> 00:23:34,320
Try it.

295
00:23:37,120 --> 00:23:38,320
I can do this myself.

296
00:23:39,280 --> 00:23:40,320
Just drink it.

297
00:23:48,280 --> 00:23:49,360
What do you think?

298
00:23:51,520 --> 00:23:52,840
It's good.

299
00:23:54,000 --> 00:23:55,440
I'll give you a shopping list tomorrow.

300
00:23:55,520 --> 00:23:57,120
Let's furnish the kitchen.

301
00:23:57,960 --> 00:24:01,000
You know I don't cook here.

302
00:24:03,480 --> 00:24:04,760
I can when I'm here.

303
00:24:12,160 --> 00:24:13,360
How long are you staying here?

304
00:24:14,920 --> 00:24:15,800
Until I recover.

305
00:24:26,480 --> 00:24:27,400
Does it still hurt?

306
00:24:31,000 --> 00:24:32,240
Occasionally.

307
00:24:34,200 --> 00:24:37,320
After you eat, do some calf raises.

308
00:25:23,520 --> 00:25:24,480
So?

309
00:25:24,560 --> 00:25:26,800
How is my performance as a househusband?

310
00:25:31,800 --> 00:25:33,080
Have you peed your kidney stone out?

311
00:25:37,040 --> 00:25:38,200
I don't know.

312
00:25:38,280 --> 00:25:39,640
But it doesn't hurt as much anymore.

313
00:25:43,400 --> 00:25:44,760
Then, return to Beijing tomorrow.

314
00:25:49,440 --> 00:25:50,600
I have taken a long leave.

315
00:26:00,640 --> 00:26:01,640
Shang Zhitao.

316
00:26:03,040 --> 00:26:04,280
You told me last time

317
00:26:04,360 --> 00:26:06,120
that you were young,
so you wanted to take the risk.

318
00:26:09,680 --> 00:26:10,920
Let's take another leap of faith.

319
00:26:31,240 --> 00:26:33,480
I don't want to take the old path.

320
00:26:38,520 --> 00:26:39,440
We are not doing that.

321
00:26:40,720 --> 00:26:42,080
I'll come with you.

322
00:26:43,720 --> 00:26:44,880
You can take me anywhere you want.

323
00:26:55,480 --> 00:26:56,360
Shang Zhitao.

324
00:26:57,080 --> 00:26:58,120
Luke has missed you a lot.

325
00:26:59,080 --> 00:27:02,920
Whenever we do a video call,
Luke just rushes to me

326
00:27:03,720 --> 00:27:05,000
whenever he hears you.

327
00:27:07,400 --> 00:27:08,960
He's more honest than I am.

328
00:27:10,000 --> 00:27:11,440
So, let me be honest with you.

329
00:27:12,800 --> 00:27:14,440
After we broke up,

330
00:27:15,080 --> 00:27:16,160
I felt awful.

331
00:27:17,360 --> 00:27:19,880
It's as if I've lost
something precious to me.

332
00:27:26,240 --> 00:27:27,920
I'm not good with words.

333
00:27:29,640 --> 00:27:30,680
But I know I miss you.

334
00:27:32,080 --> 00:27:33,000
I want to see you.

335
00:27:35,120 --> 00:27:36,600
I want to take a leap of faith with you.

336
00:27:39,360 --> 00:27:41,000
I want to see
if I can make it work between us.

337
00:27:44,200 --> 00:27:46,160
I have thought about our future.

338
00:27:49,120 --> 00:27:50,760
Can we start over again?

339
00:27:53,320 --> 00:27:54,160
Tao.

340
00:27:55,200 --> 00:27:56,920
Tell me. Do you not miss me?

341
00:28:20,960 --> 00:28:22,000
You're so annoying.

342
00:28:26,240 --> 00:28:27,120
You're so annoying.

343
00:28:28,680 --> 00:28:31,160
I have missed you so much.

344
00:28:48,640 --> 00:28:49,600
Shang Zhitao.

345
00:28:51,320 --> 00:28:52,200
Come back to Beijing with me.

346
00:28:57,880 --> 00:28:58,920
Come.

347
00:28:59,680 --> 00:29:00,840
Come back to Beijing with me.

348
00:29:05,120 --> 00:29:07,320
In what capacity
are you talking to me right now?

349
00:29:12,480 --> 00:29:13,800
If you're speaking as my boyfriend,

350
00:29:14,920 --> 00:29:18,480
I'll turn you down
because I like this project a lot.

351
00:29:19,200 --> 00:29:23,360
I want to see it through,
and I hope you'll respect my choice.

352
00:29:26,120 --> 00:29:28,400
If you're speaking as my boss,

353
00:29:30,440 --> 00:29:33,000
then I'll come back.
Because you're my boss.

354
00:29:34,600 --> 00:29:36,560
But I think it's a shame.

355
00:29:37,280 --> 00:29:39,000
I don't know

356
00:29:39,080 --> 00:29:41,560
if I'll ever have
a similar opportunity again in the future.

357
00:29:41,640 --> 00:29:44,640
This is the only shot
that will most likely change my life.

358
00:30:06,760 --> 00:30:08,200
<i>Let's travel together.</i>

359
00:30:08,920 --> 00:30:10,080
<i>Where to?</i>

360
00:30:11,280 --> 00:30:13,440
<i>We'll bring the dog with us</i>
<i>and go wherever we want.</i>

361
00:30:30,280 --> 00:30:31,880
Where are we going next?

362
00:30:34,040 --> 00:30:34,880
To Tibet, China.

363
00:30:36,560 --> 00:30:37,440
Tibet, China?

364
00:30:39,760 --> 00:30:41,200
What if I have altitude sickness?

365
00:30:42,640 --> 00:30:44,000
We have oxygen bottles.

366
00:30:44,600 --> 00:30:47,760
If I have altitude sickness,
will you look after me?

367
00:30:47,840 --> 00:30:49,040
If you have altitude sickness,

368
00:30:50,560 --> 00:30:52,120
I'll sell you off.

369
00:31:00,120 --> 00:31:01,800
- It's dangerous.
- Come here.

370
00:31:08,920 --> 00:31:10,000
Why are you staring at me?

371
00:31:13,080 --> 00:31:17,040
You are so gentle today.

372
00:31:19,480 --> 00:31:20,840
Have I ever hit you?

373
00:31:20,920 --> 00:31:22,160
No.

374
00:31:23,320 --> 00:31:25,040
I just wish you could be

375
00:31:26,400 --> 00:31:28,200
this gentle with me more often.

376
00:31:31,800 --> 00:31:33,120
So you like someone who's soft.

377
00:31:34,560 --> 00:31:35,720
Luan Nian.

378
00:31:35,800 --> 00:31:37,000
Do you know?

379
00:31:37,080 --> 00:31:38,800
I think you should know this.

380
00:31:39,800 --> 00:31:41,040
What?

381
00:31:42,000 --> 00:31:43,960
I love to travel with you.

382
00:31:46,080 --> 00:31:47,280
That's all?

383
00:31:47,800 --> 00:31:49,520
Anything you want to add?

384
00:31:58,160 --> 00:31:59,120
Luan Nian.

385
00:32:01,280 --> 00:32:03,360
<i>I love every path you take.</i>

386
00:32:06,040 --> 00:32:07,520
<i>I love to go on an adventure with you.</i>

387
00:32:10,680 --> 00:32:12,360
<i>I love the landscape on this journey.</i>

388
00:32:13,520 --> 00:32:15,360
<i>Because we're doing it together.</i>

389
00:32:52,200 --> 00:32:54,360
MOM

390
00:32:54,440 --> 00:32:56,720
- It's my mom.
- Pick it up.

391
00:32:58,680 --> 00:32:59,560
Mom.

392
00:32:59,640 --> 00:33:02,680
<i>Why didn't you go on the trip</i>
<i>with Song Qiuhan and the rest?</i>

393
00:33:03,720 --> 00:33:05,520
I changed my mind. I have a road trip now.

394
00:33:06,240 --> 00:33:07,280
A road trip?

395
00:33:08,480 --> 00:33:09,360
With Flora?

396
00:33:10,360 --> 00:33:11,640
You sure have a good memory.

397
00:33:12,480 --> 00:33:13,680
I'm driving. I'll call you back

398
00:33:13,760 --> 00:33:16,800
- when we take a break in the city.
- <i>No need.</i>

399
00:33:16,880 --> 00:33:18,720
You're having fun right now.

400
00:33:18,800 --> 00:33:20,000
No need to call me.

401
00:33:20,080 --> 00:33:22,960
<i>Just text me to tell me you're safe.</i>

402
00:33:24,360 --> 00:33:25,480
Flora.

403
00:33:26,920 --> 00:33:28,280
Yes, Dr. Liang?

404
00:33:28,360 --> 00:33:30,000
Luan Nian has a bad temper.

405
00:33:30,600 --> 00:33:33,120
<i>And he can be quite weird.</i>
<i>Thank you for putting up with him.</i>

406
00:33:33,200 --> 00:33:35,480
<i>But don't take it lying down.</i>

407
00:33:35,560 --> 00:33:37,320
- <i>If he does something wrong, you--</i>
- Anyway.

408
00:33:37,400 --> 00:33:40,160
I have a good temper. And I am not weird.

409
00:33:40,840 --> 00:33:41,840
Bye.

410
00:33:45,920 --> 00:33:47,400
Not weird, you said?

411
00:33:52,920 --> 00:33:55,640
I think our son is in love.

412
00:33:55,720 --> 00:33:58,720
And I think he really loves her.

413
00:34:01,480 --> 00:34:03,440
It's just a trip. How is it real?

414
00:34:03,960 --> 00:34:06,560
He was with Zang Yao for a decade.
Did he fall in love with her?

415
00:34:08,159 --> 00:34:09,400
Honestly,

416
00:34:09,480 --> 00:34:13,159
businessmen like you
only know how to do business.

417
00:34:14,159 --> 00:34:16,400
Has he ever gone out with Zang Yao alone?

418
00:34:17,520 --> 00:34:18,719
Also,

419
00:34:18,800 --> 00:34:22,360
Luan Nian even admitted
that she was his girlfriend.

420
00:34:22,440 --> 00:34:23,320
Has he ever done that?

421
00:34:24,719 --> 00:34:27,920
You are just too eager
to be a grandmother.

422
00:34:28,960 --> 00:34:30,080
Listen.

423
00:34:30,159 --> 00:34:31,600
Don't be too eager.

424
00:34:32,120 --> 00:34:34,440
Don't get your hopes up

425
00:34:34,520 --> 00:34:36,480
because Luan Nian
has always been like this.

426
00:34:36,560 --> 00:34:39,600
- He will mess things up.
- And he got that from you.

427
00:34:41,159 --> 00:34:42,600
If only he were more like me.

428
00:35:42,360 --> 00:35:43,600
Do you want to take photos?

429
00:35:43,680 --> 00:35:44,680
You can pick your costumes inside.

430
00:35:45,400 --> 00:35:46,520
Let me see.

431
00:35:51,320 --> 00:35:54,560
Luan Nian. Do you like the photos here?

432
00:35:55,120 --> 00:35:55,960
I do.

433
00:35:56,480 --> 00:35:57,680
But I won't take them.

434
00:36:01,160 --> 00:36:02,200
Sir.

435
00:36:02,280 --> 00:36:03,920
Do you… Do you have a model here?

436
00:36:04,800 --> 00:36:07,320
A male model
to take a couple of photos with me.

437
00:36:07,960 --> 00:36:09,360
Yes.

438
00:36:09,440 --> 00:36:10,880
You just have to pay extra.

439
00:36:10,960 --> 00:36:12,200
Let me show you.

440
00:36:12,280 --> 00:36:13,600
Young Tibetan men.

441
00:36:13,680 --> 00:36:15,080
- Really?
- They are very handsome.

442
00:36:15,160 --> 00:36:16,920
I want a handsome one

443
00:36:17,000 --> 00:36:18,680
- to take photos, like--
- Shang Zhitao.

444
00:36:24,240 --> 00:36:25,240
Which one do you want?

445
00:36:27,960 --> 00:36:28,880
You pick one first.

446
00:36:49,840 --> 00:36:51,160
Okay. Great.

447
00:36:52,000 --> 00:36:53,160
Stay.

448
00:36:53,240 --> 00:36:54,240
Hold it higher.

449
00:36:54,320 --> 00:36:56,440
Yes! Great. This is good.

450
00:36:59,200 --> 00:37:00,680
Two more single photos.

451
00:37:02,520 --> 00:37:03,960
Your husband can join now.

452
00:37:14,040 --> 00:37:16,080
- Stand here?
- Yes.

453
00:37:20,760 --> 00:37:22,360
Stand closer to your wife.

454
00:37:26,240 --> 00:37:29,040
Yes. Hug your wife.

455
00:37:31,760 --> 00:37:32,600
Yes.

456
00:37:34,000 --> 00:37:36,200
Don't be so stiff, you two.

457
00:37:36,280 --> 00:37:38,240
Just relax.

458
00:37:39,680 --> 00:37:42,120
Too stiff. Aren't you always
soft and relaxed?

459
00:37:47,640 --> 00:37:49,920
Wonderful. Good.

460
00:37:50,600 --> 00:37:53,200
Closer. Yes!

461
00:38:10,560 --> 00:38:12,880
Good. Let's pick your photos here.

462
00:38:23,480 --> 00:38:24,520
Come here already.

463
00:38:30,200 --> 00:38:31,440
<i>So gentle.</i>

464
00:38:31,520 --> 00:38:33,280
<i>Is this the Luan Nian I know?</i>

465
00:38:34,520 --> 00:38:37,520
<i>It feels like</i>
<i>we're dating for real this time.</i>

466
00:38:53,600 --> 00:38:54,480
Eat now, Luke.

467
00:38:57,240 --> 00:38:59,560
He's so fat now. Stop feeding him.

468
00:38:59,640 --> 00:39:00,480
Drink some water.

469
00:39:02,200 --> 00:39:03,280
Thanks.

470
00:39:12,480 --> 00:39:16,520
I appreciate that you never
threw tantrums at me.

471
00:39:16,600 --> 00:39:19,720
You didn't leave me behind on the streets.

472
00:39:19,800 --> 00:39:20,760
Congratulations.

473
00:39:20,840 --> 00:39:24,000
You have become someone I trust.

474
00:39:26,160 --> 00:39:28,760
- That's my honor.
- Of course.

475
00:39:37,160 --> 00:39:40,320
- Mom.
- <i>How is Tibet, China?</i>

476
00:39:40,400 --> 00:39:41,880
I love it here.

477
00:39:41,960 --> 00:39:44,360
I eat well. I sleep well.

478
00:39:44,440 --> 00:39:45,520
The scenery here is beautiful.

479
00:39:46,440 --> 00:39:47,520
Luke is happy too.

480
00:39:50,720 --> 00:39:52,200
Who are you traveling with?

481
00:39:52,280 --> 00:39:53,800
Your boyfriend?

482
00:39:56,440 --> 00:39:58,400
Yes. My boyfriend.

483
00:40:02,040 --> 00:40:03,960
When did this happen?

484
00:40:04,040 --> 00:40:05,760
- Who is he?
- Yes. Who?

485
00:40:05,840 --> 00:40:07,120
How is his family?

486
00:40:07,200 --> 00:40:09,000
How are his parents?

487
00:40:09,080 --> 00:40:10,080
Is he kind?

488
00:40:10,880 --> 00:40:12,760
Hi, Mrs. Shang. I am Luan Nian.

489
00:40:17,960 --> 00:40:22,600
Hi. We are on the phone
together with Tao's dad.

490
00:40:22,680 --> 00:40:24,240
- <i>You are Mr. Luan, right?</i>
- Give me that.

491
00:40:24,320 --> 00:40:25,200
Yes, Mrs. Shang.

492
00:40:25,280 --> 00:40:26,960
Tao and I have been dating for six years.

493
00:40:29,240 --> 00:40:30,320
My family is okay.

494
00:40:30,400 --> 00:40:31,480
- My annual income is--
- Enough.

495
00:40:32,760 --> 00:40:34,160
Mom. I…

496
00:40:34,240 --> 00:40:36,080
I'll talk to you later. Bye.

497
00:40:37,400 --> 00:40:38,480
He hasn't even finished.

498
00:40:41,720 --> 00:40:43,160
Why are you scared?

499
00:40:43,240 --> 00:40:44,120
Too ashamed to tell anyone?

500
00:40:44,200 --> 00:40:45,680
No.

501
00:40:45,760 --> 00:40:47,360
I just…

502
00:40:51,160 --> 00:40:52,120
Yes?

503
00:41:04,280 --> 00:41:05,560
Luan Nian.

504
00:41:11,480 --> 00:41:12,400
What?

505
00:41:33,360 --> 00:41:34,440
Luke is here.

506
00:41:38,440 --> 00:41:40,080
And you have altitude sickness. Be nice.

507
00:41:46,880 --> 00:41:48,800
I think I'm fine.

508
00:41:48,880 --> 00:41:50,040
I don't have altitude sickness.

509
00:41:50,120 --> 00:41:51,520
Right.

510
00:41:53,040 --> 00:41:55,440
Smooth your breathing first.

511
00:41:56,640 --> 00:41:59,080
If something happens to you,
I'll have to collect your body.

512
00:42:01,360 --> 00:42:03,320
Then, can we talk?

513
00:42:05,520 --> 00:42:06,360
About what?

514
00:42:09,360 --> 00:42:10,760
Let's talk

515
00:42:11,680 --> 00:42:13,360
about the first time we met.

516
00:42:15,760 --> 00:42:17,280
The first time we met?

517
00:42:19,240 --> 00:42:20,080
In the office?

518
00:42:20,880 --> 00:42:22,480
No.

519
00:42:22,560 --> 00:42:23,480
You don't remember?

520
00:42:23,560 --> 00:42:24,760
Where was it then?

521
00:42:24,840 --> 00:42:26,120
In the hall.

522
00:42:26,920 --> 00:42:31,560
I was like, how could someone
be this handsome?

523
00:42:31,640 --> 00:42:33,720
You're the most handsome man I've met.

524
00:42:34,320 --> 00:42:35,680
Your turn now.

525
00:42:35,760 --> 00:42:36,680
Tell me.

526
00:42:38,000 --> 00:42:41,800
When I first met you, I was thinking,
how could someone be this dumb?

527
00:42:44,560 --> 00:42:46,440
Like a big dummy.

528
00:42:50,040 --> 00:42:50,960
I'm tired now.

529
00:42:52,760 --> 00:42:54,160
- Mad?
- No.

530
00:42:54,240 --> 00:42:55,240
I'm just sleepy.

531
00:42:56,920 --> 00:42:57,920
Shang Zhitao.

532
00:42:59,760 --> 00:43:01,240
Should we catch the aurora next year?

533
00:43:04,640 --> 00:43:05,960
I'll go

534
00:43:07,200 --> 00:43:08,840
wherever you go.

535
00:43:18,560 --> 00:43:22,240
<i>This year is a good year.</i>

536
00:43:40,040 --> 00:43:41,200
I love this photo.

537
00:43:42,400 --> 00:43:43,800
This one too.

538
00:43:45,200 --> 00:43:46,440
This one is good.

539
00:43:46,520 --> 00:43:49,840
This one is good.
You're a good photographer.

540
00:43:50,720 --> 00:43:51,680
Thank you.

541
00:43:51,760 --> 00:43:53,080
I want all of them.

542
00:43:53,160 --> 00:43:54,280
We'll take everything then.

543
00:43:54,360 --> 00:43:55,440
How much more should we pay?

544
00:43:56,160 --> 00:43:57,160
No need to pay extra.

545
00:43:57,240 --> 00:43:59,560
Can I hang one in my shop?

546
00:43:59,640 --> 00:44:00,840
Then, you'll have to pay us.

547
00:44:05,200 --> 00:44:06,520
Pick one

548
00:44:06,600 --> 00:44:08,040
and hang it
at the most visible place in the shop.

549
00:44:08,120 --> 00:44:09,720
Process it with the best film.

550
00:44:09,800 --> 00:44:11,000
Once you're done, I'll inspect it.

551
00:44:11,080 --> 00:44:13,040
Sure. No problem.

552
00:44:13,120 --> 00:44:14,640
I'll give you the original film.

553
00:44:14,720 --> 00:44:17,240
After I process it,
you can pick two as your wedding photos.

554
00:44:18,200 --> 00:44:19,520
It'll last for many years.

555
00:44:20,080 --> 00:44:22,520
The Tibetans use this
for their wedding photos.

556
00:44:24,120 --> 00:44:26,800
I highly doubt I can get
good photos like this again.

557
00:44:27,640 --> 00:44:28,600
Of course.

558
00:44:31,800 --> 00:44:33,320
I'll count on you
to process the films, then.

559
00:44:33,400 --> 00:44:34,400
Sure. Don't worry.

560
00:44:35,440 --> 00:44:36,360
Luan Nian.
